WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.000
House of the Dragon, Game of Thrones prequel
series that will air next year, is currently

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.650
filming on multiple locations and while filming
is happening, we have more actors and more

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:15.860
roles revealed and therefore we have more
character explaining to do. House of the Dragon,

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:21.180
although based on George RR Martin's Targaryen
history book Fire &amp; Blood, will not feature

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:26.330
Targaryens only, but many other houses and
many other legendary figures from that time

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:31.570
period as well. While the cast for most of
the main characters was already announced

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:37.300
such as those for Viserys, Aegon, Daemon and
Rhaenyra Targaryen as well as for Otto and

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:43.159
Alicent Hightower, and Corlys Velaryion, one
of the most important characters in the story

00:00:43.159 --> 00:00:49.050
has recently been announced by none other
than George R.R. Martin himself. Martin announced

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:54.139
the newest casting for House of the Dragon
and the role is for the Kingmaker, Ser Criston

00:00:54.139 --> 00:01:00.019
Cole, who will be played by Fabien Frankel.
Martin gave the following description of the

00:01:00.019 --> 00:01:02.940
character:
Cole plays a key role in the Dance of the

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.990
Dragons, as his nickname hints.
He’s the common-born son of the steward

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:13.909
to the Lord of Blackhaven. He’s got no claim
to lands or titles, all he has is an honor

00:01:13.909 --> 00:01:19.530
and his skill with sword and lance. He’s
a challenger, a champion, cheered by the commons,

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:25.119
beloved of the ladies. He’s a lover (or
is he?), a seducer (or is he?), a betrayer

00:01:25.119 --> 00:01:30.659
(or is he?), a breaker of hearts, and a maker
of kings. I can tell you that Ser Criston

00:01:30.659 --> 00:01:35.369
Cole is one of those characters that you will
love and hate, which in my opinion is the

00:01:35.369 --> 00:01:40.759
best type of character. Criston is a complex
character. He's one of the best knights of

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:45.539
his time, Lord Commander of the Kingsguard
and as the story progresses, he even becomes

00:01:45.539 --> 00:01:50.149
the Hand of the King. At the beginning of
our story, he's loyal friend and protector

00:01:50.149 --> 00:01:56.350
of Princess Rhaenyra, but later, upon some
mysterious events, he changes his allegiance

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:02.329
to Queen Alicent, Rhaenyra's enemy at King's
Landing court and later serves King Aegon

00:02:02.329 --> 00:02:07.570
and fights against Rhaenyra during the entire
civil war. The Targaryen civil war is the

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:12.470
key event of this show as it's the key in
a history of House Targaryen, the Dance of

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:17.400
the Dragons which divided Westeros in two
and launched a huge war.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:23.830
A war of succession between Aegon II and his
half-sister Rhaenyra over their father Viserys

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:28.110
I's throne.
It made House Targaryen much weaker, especially

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:33.230
because this conflict resulted with the extinction
of their dragons, while its numbers were at

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:38.970
its peak at the war's start. Miguel Sapochnik
and Ryan Condal will serve as showrunners

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:45.030
and executive producers. George R. R. Martin
will also serve as executive producer. Back

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:50.220
to Ser Criston Cole and his importance in
all of this. Ser Criston Cole was a knight

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:56.200
from House Cole. Made a member of King Viserys
I Targaryen's Kingsguard, eventually rising

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:01.860
to Lord Commander. Criston convinced Viserys's
son, Aegon, to claim the rule of the Seven

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:08.020
Kingdoms as his father lay dead. This led
to the Dance of the Dragons, a civil war between

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:15.120
Aegon II and his elder sister, Rhaenyra, whom
Viserys had long trained as his successor.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:21.450
For this, he became known as Criston the Kingmaker.
He was an exceptionally skilled warrior, especially

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:27.010
with his morningstar. Criston appears in the
history of House Targaryen by winning a melee

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:32.710
at the tourney at Maidenpool to celebrate
the ascension of Viserys I Targaryen, drawing

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:37.780
the attention of the royal court by knocking
Dark Sister from the hands of Prince Daemon

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:43.170
Targaryen with his morningstar. He gave the
victor's laurel to seven-year-old Princess

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:49.460
Rhaenyra Targaryen, whose favor he wore while
unhorsing Daemon in the joust, as well as

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:55.320
the famed Cargyll twins of the Kingsguard,
before being unhorsed by Lord Lymond Mallister.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:04:02.350
Thereafter, King Viserys indulged Rhaenyra
by naming Criston her personal sworn shield.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:07.330
In 105 AC, the twenty-three-year-old Criston
became a member of the Kingsguard, taking

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:13.430
the place of the legendary Ser Ryam Redwyne.
Cole wore Rhaenyra's favor in a tournament

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:20.270
in 111 AC where he unhorsed Ser Gwayne Hightower,
younger brother and champion to King Viserys's

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:26.430
second wife and queen, Alicent Hightower.
In 112 AC Ser Criston was still Rhaenyra's

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:32.780
champion and constant companion. Lord Commander
Ser Harrold Westerling died in that year,

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:37.790
and Criston was named his successor to lead
the White Cloaks. It was rumored that Cole

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:44.150
had an affair with Rhaenyra in 113 AC. Septon
Eustace says that Ser Criston slipped into

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:49.670
Rhaenyra's bed-chamber to confess his love,
offering to escape the Kingsguard life with

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:55.410
her to one of the Free Cities where he would
pledge his sword to some merchant prince.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:05:01.230
Eustace also says that Rhaenyra refused him,
saying a Targaryen was meant to be more than

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:06.770
a wife of a sellsword, and that if he could
forget his Kingsguard vows, he could forget

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:13.440
marriage vows. The royal fool Mushroom tells
a different tale - that Rhaenyra had been

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.920
practicing her enticements with her uncle,
Prince Daemon, so that she would lose her

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:25.440
maidenhead to Criston, a man she loved, rather
than her betrothed cousin, Laenor Velaryon.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:30.790
She failed to seduce Ser Criston in White
Sword Tower, however, and the spurned princess

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:36.740
took solace in Ser Harwin "Breakbones" Strong.
This is why even if you read the book Fire

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:41.430
And Blood, on which this prequel is based,
you still will not know how most of the stories

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:46.690
play out because the book is not the actual
history, but the history that the author wrote

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:52.740
using many different statements. While the
author does offer few possible scenarios,

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:57.050
it doesn't mean any of them are true because
none of them were in the room with Rhaenyra

00:05:57.050 --> 00:06:02.020
and Criston. It's just what they were told
that happened. Whatever the way of it, Cole

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:08.190
went from being her most loyal defender to
her bitterest foe, and Rhaenyra soon left

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:12.350
for Driftmark with Breakbones as her new sworn
shield.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:19.060
In 114 AC, Ser Criston, as the Kingsguard
to King Viserys, attended the wedding of Rhaenyra

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:25.100
to Laenor, which included seven days of feasting
and jousting. Cole fought with Queen Alicent's

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:31.250
token, and during a melee left Breakbones
with a broken collarbone and shattered elbow,

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:36.030
thereafter prompting Mushroom to call him
"Brokenbones". Criston's morningstar also

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:41.680
cracked the helm of the Knight of Kisses,
Laenor's favorite Ser Joffrey Lonmouth, who

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:47.720
died from six days later. While many were
angered at Criston for this, including King

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:53.100
Viserys, Queen Alicent did not share their
displeasure and asked that he be made her

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:59.420
personal sworn shield. Cole thus became a
staunch supporter of Queen Alicent. Criston

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:05.480
tutored Alicent's fierce son, Prince Aemond
Targaryen to be a skilled swordsman, despite

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:12.669
Aemond having only one eye left after Rhaenyra's
son wounded him in a fight. Due to contradictory

00:07:12.669 --> 00:07:19.190
sources, Criston's motives in supporting Aegon
II are unclear; some say that he acted from

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:25.190
ambition - as Aegon was more controllable
than his willful half-sister Rhaenyra; indeed

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:30.570
Aegon II eventually raised Criston to the
office of Hand of the King. However, some

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:37.030
say Rhaenyra rejected him, adding a personal
dimension to the conflict. Others allow Cole

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:42.600
nobler motives and claim he was defending
ancient Andal custom giving precedence to

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:48.430
sons over daughters OR that he did not wish
to see Rhaenyra's children who he believed

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:54.830
to be children born out of wedlock to inherit
the Iron Throne. In any event, many of the

00:07:54.830 --> 00:08:00.020
lords of the realm were aware of Viserys's
wish to have Rhaenyra succeed him as House

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:05.919
Targaryen's first ruling queen, and stood
behind the princess after King Viserys died,

00:08:05.919 --> 00:08:12.020
most notable of which were Corlys Velaryion
and Cregan Stark. Again due to contradictory

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:17.620
sources, during the meeting of Viserys's small
council after King Viserys's death in 129

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:23.760
AC, Cole is noted to have either slit the
throat or threw from a window, the aged Lord

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:29.280
Lyman Beesbury, the only member of the council
to support crowning Princess Rhaenyra instead

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:35.819
of Prince Aegon. The rest of the council were
allies of Ser Otto and Queen Alicent Hightower.

00:08:35.819 --> 00:08:41.289
Criston later crowned Aegon II with the iron-and-ruby
crown of Aegon the Conqueror.

00:08:41.289 --> 00:08:46.379
However, Rhaenyra, who was at Dragonstone
at the time of her father's death and Aegon's

00:08:46.379 --> 00:08:52.410
coronation, refused to support Aegon, beginning
the great armed conflict which engulfed the

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:58.200
Seven Kingdoms and became known as the Dance
of the Dragons. As Rhaenyra's supporters gathered

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:05.730
their forces, Aegon II became frustrated with
his grandfather and Hand, Ser Otto Hightower,

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:11.439
and awarded the office to Criston Cole. The
Kingmaker's forces quickly took Duskendale

00:09:11.439 --> 00:09:17.600
and Rook's Rest, the latter after a fierce
battle. When Prince Aemond Targaryen became

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:23.371
Protector of the Realm and Prince Regent because
of Aegon's injuries in the battle, Criston

00:09:23.371 --> 00:09:29.749
remained the Hand. Aemond and the Kingmaker
led an army of 4,000 greens from King's Landing

00:09:29.749 --> 00:09:34.930
to retake Harrenhal in the riverlands from
Prince Daemon Targaryen, who abandoned the

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:40.980
castle before Criston arrived and took this
opportunity to take King's Landing.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:46.040
After hearing that Cregan Stark's Winter Wolfs
defeated his biggest allies, the Lannisters

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:51.540
in the battle by the Lakeshore, Aemond began
burning the riverlands and Cole marched his

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:58.399
remaining 3,600 greens south along the western
shore of the Gods Eye, intending to join with

00:09:58.399 --> 00:10:04.059
the army of Lord Ormund Hightower. However,
the Kingmaker's forces were ambushed by the

00:10:04.059 --> 00:10:09.779
Winter Wolves and river knights south of the
Gods Eye. Criston's forces were outnumbered

00:10:09.779 --> 00:10:15.309
2 to 1 by the forces of the riverlands and
the north. Criston held a parley with the

00:10:15.309 --> 00:10:22.410
Winter Wolf's commander Lord Roderick Dustin,
Ser Pate of Longleaf, and Ser Garibald Grey.

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:29.200
Criston offered to surrender but was refused
by three blacks. Upon this refusal, Ser Criston,

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:34.569
a famed knight who was also the Lord Commander
of the Kingsguard for Aegon II in addition

00:10:34.569 --> 00:10:40.590
to being the King's Hand, prepared to fight
all three of his counterparts at once. Before

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:46.579
he could do so, however, the Kingmaker was
struck down by arrows fired by Red Robb Rivers

00:10:46.579 --> 00:10:52.589
and two of his longbowmen. With Criston dead,
Lord Dustin sounded the charge of Winter Wolfs

00:10:52.589 --> 00:10:58.399
and the river knights into Criston's now leaderless
army which quickly collapsed. Perhaps we could

00:10:58.399 --> 00:11:03.459
end Criston's story with this quote about
him by Jaime Lannister. When Loras Tyrell

00:11:03.459 --> 00:11:08.930
told him that the best Kingsguard heroes will
always be remembered, Jaime replied with "the

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:14.589
best and the worst. And a few who were a bit
of both. Like Criston Cole." Was Criston in

00:11:14.589 --> 00:11:19.920
love with Rhaenyra who became her worst enemy
after she refused him or did he refuse her

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:26.480
and sided with Aegon, was Cole an honorable
knight or ambitious man with no morals, and

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:31.490
was he truly the best warrior of his time,
even better than Daemon himself? All of that

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:35.519
and more we'll see in the upcoming Game of
Thrones prequel series, House of the Dragon,

00:11:35.519 --> 00:11:40.150
which airs next year on HBO. Thank you so
much for watching and I hope to see you in

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:40.153
the next one!

